WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.596
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:08.119
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.419 --> 00:00:13.893
Unit seventeen: Crime and Safety. In this unit, you will talk about crime, safety and prevention.

4
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:15.710
crime rate.

5
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.002
crime rate means the number of crimes in a place.

6
00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:21.499
The crime rate in the city has fallen this year.

7
00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:24.317
Your turn. Say: crime rate.

8
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.065
crime rate.

9
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:29.714
theft.

10
00:00:30.414 --> 00:00:32.321
theft means the crime of stealing.

11
00:00:32.621 --> 00:00:35.015
Phone theft is common in crowded markets.

12
00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:37.648
Your turn. Say: theft.

13
00:00:40.348 --> 00:00:40.966
theft.

14
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:42.812
scam.

15
00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:46.440
scam means a dishonest plan to get money from people.

16
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.005
Don't answer messages that promise free money: it's a scam.

17
00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:53.079
Your turn. Say: scam.

18
00:00:55.779 --> 00:00:56.641
scam.

19
00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:58.547
CCTV.

20
00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:03.197
CCTV means video cameras that record public places for security.

21
00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:05.159
The thief was caught on CCTV.

22
00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:08.291
Your turn. Say: CCTV.

23
00:01:10.991 --> 00:01:11.876
CCTV.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:13.815
burglary.

25
00:01:14.515 --> 00:01:17.490
burglary means the crime of entering a building to steal.

26
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.975
There was a burglary at the shop last night.

27
00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:23.269
Your turn. Say: burglary.

28
00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:26.901
burglary.

29
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:28.697
victim.

30
00:01:29.397 --> 00:01:32.384
victim means a person who is hurt or harmed by a crime.

31
00:01:32.684 --> 00:01:35.055
The victim reported the crime to the police.

32
00:01:35.755 --> 00:01:37.977
Your turn. Say: victim.

33
00:01:40.677 --> 00:01:41.551
victim.

34
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.783
report a crime.

35
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:47.214
report a crime means to tell the police about a crime.

36
00:01:47.514 --> 00:01:50.129
You can report a crime online or at a police station.

37
00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:53.447
Your turn. Say: report a crime.

38
00:01:56.147 --> 00:01:57.484
report a crime.

39
00:01:58.483 --> 00:01:59.589
online fraud.

40
00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:04.123
online fraud means a crime where someone tricks you on the internet to get money.

41
00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.991
Online fraud is increasing around the world.

42
00:02:07.691 --> 00:02:10.425
Your turn. Say: online fraud.

43
00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:14.451
online fraud.

44
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.508
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.808 --> 00:02:20.968
My neighbour was a victim of online fraud last week.

46
00:02:22.283 --> 00:02:24.680
That's terrible. Did she report the crime?

47
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:30.238
Yes. The police said the money might be returned, but they weren't sure.

48
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.329
These scams must be stopped. People should be taught how to recognise them.

49
00:02:36.617 --> 00:02:40.973
Our building has CCTV now, so burglary should be prevented too.

50
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:45.458
Good. Crime can be reduced if everyone is careful.

51
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.585
Grammar focus: Passive with modals.

52
00:02:49.885 --> 00:02:53.859
Use a modal plus be plus past participle to make the passive with modals.

53
00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.236
For example: crime can be reduced, and scams must be reported.

54
00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:01.279
It is common in rules, notices and advice.

55
00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:07.375
Use this structure for rules, possibilities and advice when the action is more important than the person.

56
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:10.954
Now read and listen. Staying Safe Online.

57
00:03:11.254 --> 00:03:14.868
Online fraud has become one of the fastest-growing crimes in Asia.

58
00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:20.029
Many scams are sent as text messages that look like they come from a bank.

59
00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:24.872
Victims are often asked to click a link and enter their password.

60
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:29.901
Experts say that suspicious messages should be deleted immediately.

61
00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:35.190
Every scam should be reported, because it can help protect other people.

62
00:03:36.483 --> 00:03:38.915
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:39.215 --> 00:03:40.959
The crime of stealing is blank.

64
00:03:41.259 --> 00:03:44.193
A, theft. B, victim. C, CCTV.

65
00:03:48.183 --> 00:03:49.997
The answer is A: theft.

66
00:03:51.483 --> 00:03:53.878
Your password should blank every few months.

67
00:03:54.178 --> 00:03:57.216
A, change. B, be changed. C, changed.

68
00:04:01.217 --> 00:04:03.077
The answer is B: be changed.

69
00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:06.687
These rules must blank by all students.

70
00:04:06.987 --> 00:04:10.165
A, be followed. B, follow. C, following.

71
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.848
The answer is A: be followed.

72
00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.698
A dishonest plan to get money is a blank.

73
00:04:19.998 --> 00:04:23.640
A, scam. B, crime rate. C, burglary.

74
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.255
The answer is A: scam.

75
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.841
According to the text, suspicious messages should be blank.

76
00:04:34.141 --> 00:04:37.202
A, answered. B, deleted. C, shared.

77
00:04:41.217 --> 00:04:42.752
The answer is B: deleted.

78
00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.412
Now it's your turn to speak. What can people do to stay safe in a big city?

79
00:04:53.712 --> 00:04:58.532
Bags should be kept close to your body, and phones shouldn't be left on café tables.

80
00:04:58.832 --> 00:05:00.391
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:01.383 --> 00:05:05.348
Great work today! You learned eight new words and passive with modals.

82
00:05:05.648 --> 00:05:09.333
Today's value is safety. Be careful near cars and roads.

83
00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:12.042
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:12.342 --> 00:05:15.099
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

